# CANON — keep this entry, and understand that it is now load-bearing. Hole 3
# puts `pnpm format` at the end of `changeset:version`, and the format glob
# `**/*.{ts,tsx,json,md}` reaches this file, so without this entry the formatter
# would rewrite a file the standard says is copied verbatim — on every version
# run, silently. That is the defect ticket 13 found in jperezmart/config.
#
# Ticket 20 measured it as precautionary: the canon's longest line is 99
# characters, and against the repo's old `printWidth` of 100 Prettier left it
# alone. **One character of margin.** Ticket 22 spent that margin. Adopting
# `@jperezmart/prettier-config` moved `printWidth` to 80, and the line that
# carries the repo name — `"changelog": [..., { "repo":
# "jperezmart/radix-themes-devtools-ts" }]` — now reflows onto four lines.
# Measured, not assumed: remove this entry and `pnpm format` rewrites the canon
# on the next `changeset:version`.
#
# The shared config also ships `prettier-plugin-sort-json`. That was expected to
# be a second, independent rewrite, and measuring it says otherwise: the canon's
# ten keys are already in the plugin's output order, so today it is a no-op.
# Recorded as a latent risk rather than a live one — a key added out of order
# would wake it, and unlike `printWidth` no line length would warn first.
#
# `release.yml` needs no entry: the same glob excludes YAML.
.changeset/config.json

